{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e","id":822169,"title":"How exclusive is Tribe membership in 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-02T23:45:42-08:00","id":822169,"title":"How exclusive is Tribe membership in 2E?","content":"1e werewolf mentioned there being tests you had to pass in order to be accepted into a tribe, but I don't see anything for that in 2e. Is that still a thing, or is membership more open now? If someone can be excluded from joining a tribe, then on what basis could they be so?<br /> <br /> Is being a member of a tribe as simple as claiming membership in it? Is there a central authority determining who is or isn't part of a tribe?<br /> <br /> Can you be excluded because said authority or other tribe members think you don't fit the mindset of the group? What about personal conflicts? If all or most of the local members of a tribe just decide they don't like you (Maybe you're an asshole. Maybe you're really off-putting) would that be enough for them to say &quot;you can't run with us.&quot;<br /> <br /> I get that Uratha politics are going to vary from region to region, but I'm looking for a general idea of how you can expect tribal politics to function now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:33:57-08:00","id":822419,"title":"","content":"In my games they still have to undergo a trial. It's more interesting that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T08:49:29-08:00","id":822432,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that if you've unlocked a Gift associated with a Tribe, you're basically in like Flynn. If you haven't, you can still <i>claim</i> that you're in a Tribe, and if you're knowledgeable enough about how things work you can even dedicate Rites and prayers to the Firstborn totem, but there's no central authority who can verify your membership: if you have Tribal Status that would indicate that the other tribe members in the area recognize you as a real &quot;member&quot;, and you'd have some sway with spirits related to the Tribe.<br /> <br /> An initiation trial or ritual would be a good justification for having any amount of Status.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T11:57:36-08:00","id":822572,"title":"","content":"I play it as, if you buy a dot of status then you get to be part of the tribe from the beginning. Otherwise you start life as a Ghost Wolf. But those are house rules so...YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:02:34-08:00","id":822574,"title":"","content":"I doubt there's a central membership, but it seems like any member could initiate you into the tribe, or at least direct you to someone who could. It's something most werewolves are considered to have done during character generation, though you can use house rules like Jacob or role-play it in game. I imagine there is at least some form of formal acknowledgment, as you are accepting a ban by joining.<br /> <br /> There is apparently a book about the Tribes on the schedule somewhere, so something like that would probably be delved into there. Until then, the Tribes of the Moon book might have good advice for it if you need information about it now, though hopefully someone who knows the book more will verify that.<br /> <br /> I do think some people might think you inappropriate for recruitment, but I also think it might be something you could get around if you really wanted to. As you said it varies from region to region, and while there are <a href=\"http://www.cellphonereviews.com/images/cell-phone-evolution.png\" target=\"_blank\">things werewolves can do to communicate over long distances</a>, only the tribal totems seem to be able to reach out and touch everyone in a tribe. Making end-runs around that kind of thing are probably frowned upon, though.<br /> <br /> Spirits, specifically servants of the tribal totems, can probably induct werewolves into tribes if there's no one around to do it.<br /> <br /> As for reasons why someone might be refused entry, the obvious reason is probably not really fitting into the tribal concept. Someone who has no intention of following the tribal ban, or who is known for breaking the Oath of the Moon or other crimes might. I could see familial affiliations barring someone, but that's more of a social thing. If someone comes from a long line of zealous and insular Blood Talons or Predator Kings and runs away from home to join the Iron Masters, providing who they went to knows what's up they might tell them to talk to their family first so whoever recruits the wolf doesn't end up on the wrong end of a Sacred Hunt, though I could also see werewolves going out of their way to make a show of it and bring them in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-03-2016, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:11:06-08:00","id":822586,"title":"","content":"There's one true arbiter of Tribe membership - the totem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:17:30-08:00","id":822593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822586#post822586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one true arbiter of Tribe membership - the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>So does the tribal totem have to give assent? Based on what we've seen on them they do seem able to keep tabs on, basically, every member of their tribe at once.<br /> <br /> Our first game had Death Wolf and one of the Pure totems have a meeting in the city peacefully, at the cost of all the spiritual chaos caused from their presence. Though based on Basra it seems like we really underestimated the effect they would have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:40:40-08:00","id":822626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822586#post822586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one true arbiter of Tribe membership - the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my pre-2ED game I locked PCs in distant small town, only with pack of Bale Hounds. <b>PCs still joined proper Tribes as Firstborn appeared before them!</b> PCs still need to make Firstborn Trial to earn appropiate Tribal Renown, but could join Tribes even without other Tribes members. I say it's totally possible to be &quot;Firstborn chosen&quot; and be in Tribe only because Firstborn is likes you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T12:43:30-08:00","id":822629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822586#post822586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's one true arbiter of Tribe membership - the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>So joining a tribe would involve presenting yourself before the tribal totem and getting their approval? I always got the sense of them being rather distant and hard to reach, but maybe that was just a fault in my reading. Exactly how easy is it to make contact with one of them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T13:01:46-08:00","id":822656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822629#post822629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So joining a tribe would involve presenting yourself before the tribal totem and getting their approval? I always got the sense of them being rather distant and hard to reach, but maybe that was just a fault in my reading. Exactly how easy is it to make contact with one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div>1ED presented Firstborns and Luna as distant beings in books. Well, Firstborn <i>s</i><i>ometimes</i> shown themselves, in &quot;once in campaign&quot; event. But most of the time they looked over their Tribes children from their Places-That-Should-Not-Be in Deep Shadow.<br /> <br /> It's popular &quot;setting hack&quot; that they can be more direct and show from time to time to PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T13:05:14-08:00","id":822659,"title":"","content":"Spirits of their rank can generally send lesser avatars of themselves in their place. They could probably do something similar with just a lesser Influence, allow a wolf to howl its assent or something in the distance.<br /> <br /> In the second edition book, Basra is currently suffering from the actual presence of a Firstborn. It is not pretty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T15:04:50-08:00","id":822809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822659#post822659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirits of their rank can generally send lesser avatars of themselves in their place. They could probably do something similar with just a lesser Influence, allow a wolf to howl its assent or something in the distance.<br /> <br /> In the second edition book, Basra is currently suffering from the actual presence of a Firstborn. It is not pretty.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Destroyer Wolf lives up to its name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T15:40:13-08:00","id":822826,"title":"","content":"I don't understand - choosing a tribe is part of rolling up a character. How can you test for membership at that point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11158-avalon-polo","name":"Avalon Polo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T15:45:19-08:00","id":822830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avalon Polo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822826#post822826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand - choosing a tribe is part of rolling up a character. How can you test for membership at that point?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a test that the player has to make, necessarily. But the character themselves doesn't begin their lives as part of the tribe. They have to go through the process of joining. What I really want to know is what that looks like for the character themselves. Or not even for player characters. Just, in the world of darkness, what is the process of joining a tribe?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T15:48:46-08:00","id":822831,"title":"","content":"Oh, got it, thanks!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822830#post822830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a test that the player has to make, necessarily. But the character themselves doesn't begin their lives as part of the tribe. They have to go through the process of joining. What I really want to know is what that looks like for the character themselves. Or not even for player characters. Just, in the world of darkness, what is the process of joining a tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11158-avalon-polo","name":"Avalon Polo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T15:50:55-08:00","id":822833,"title":"","content":"Alternatively some people play mortal games that turn into werewolf games.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5686-neckbeard\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5686\" data-vbnamecard=\"5686\">Neckbeard</a> the Pirate 'I checked and Tribes of the Moon does have Joining Up sections. A common initiation for the Bone Shadows has the aspirant trying to put down a ghost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T15:53:23-08:00","id":822834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822833#post822833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively some people play mortal games that turn into werewolf games.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5686-neckbeard\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5686\" data-vbnamecard=\"5686\">Neckbeard</a> the Pirate 'I checked and Tribes of the Moon does have Joining Up sections. A common initiation for the Bone Shadows has the aspirant trying to put down a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that a post-GMC book? I don't know if I have that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T15:57:41-08:00","id":822839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822830#post822830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not a test that the player has to make, necessarily. But the character themselves doesn't begin their lives as part of the tribe. They have to go through the process of joining. What I really want to know is what that looks like for the character themselves. Or not even for player characters. Just, in the world of darkness, what is the process of joining a tribe?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively some people play mortal games that turn into werewolf games, where these things would be played out by the characters, if they didn't skip ahead.<br /> <br /> I checked and Tribes of the Moon does have Joining Up sections. A common initiation for the Bone Shadows has the aspirant trying to put down a ghost. Blood Talons have a simpler one, 'Destroy an enemy. End a conflict. Don't surrender.' Hunters in Darkness take them on a hunt. Iron Masters have to show they can think on their feet and ask questions. And Storm Lords test a variety of traits important to them. It's all first edition stuff so some may be dated.<br /> <br /> Ugh, horrible double posting on my part, sorry bout that.<br /> <br /> No it's a first edition book, it flew under my radar too originally. Tribes of the Moon covers the five tribes of the Forsaken, a chapter for each with customs, characters, lodges and rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:29:56-08:00","id":822864,"title":"","content":"Considering you gain a dot of Renown for joining up, I would assume there is some form of initiation designed to help you earn that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T16:42:02-08:00","id":822877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822839#post822839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively some people play mortal games that turn into werewolf games, where these things would be played out by the characters, if they didn't skip ahead.<br /> <br /> I checked and Tribes of the Moon does have Joining Up sections. A common initiation for the Bone Shadows has the aspirant trying to put down a ghost. Blood Talons have a simpler one, 'Destroy an enemy. End a conflict. Don't surrender.' Hunters in Darkness take them on a hunt. Iron Masters have to show they can think on their feet and ask questions. And Storm Lords test a variety of traits important to them. It's all first edition stuff so some may be dated.<br /> <br /> Ugh, horrible double posting on my part, sorry bout that.<br /> <br /> No it's a first edition book, it flew under my radar too originally. Tribes of the Moon covers the five tribes of the Forsaken, a chapter for each with customs, characters, lodges and rites.</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked it up and it's definitely helping me wrap my head around it a bit, but the tribal identities did change a bit between first and second editions, albeit subtly, so I don't know how much of it applies anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T17:22:06-08:00","id":822902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822877#post822877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked it up and it's definitely helping me wrap my head around it a bit, but the tribal identities did change a bit between first and second editions, albeit subtly, so I don't know how much of it applies anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I could see it as simple as going on a Sacred Hunt and proving yourself, or leading one. As you said in your first post, there wouldn't be one way all werewolves across the globe would manage it. Providing it was up to the tribal members to test, at least. If a Firstborn says you're in, you're in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T20:18:48-08:00","id":823006,"title":"","content":"The new werewolf characters still get's Tribal Renown. I would imply that with new Prey focus of the Tribes - each new member need to Hunt on it's Sacred Prey and in the process, get the Renown.<br /> <br /> That means that Intiation Rites for Tribes are:<ul><li><b>Blood Talons</b> - Hunting other Uratha and getting Glory at the end.</li> <li><b>Bone Shadows</b> - Hunting ephemeral being and getting Wisdom at the end.</li> <li><b>Hunters in Darkness</b> - Hunting Host and getting Purity at the end.</li> <li><b>Iron Masters</b> - Hunting human ( or even group of them ) inside mortal population and getting Cunning at the end.</li> <li><b>Storm Lords</b> - Hunting the Urged and getting Honor at the end.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T00:06:20-08:00","id":823128,"title":"","content":"I imagine Lodges to be more exclusive than Tribes, however open or not the latter might be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T07:39:21-08:00","id":823334,"title":"","content":"If I were to do 2e Tribal Initiation in my games, they would involve hunting, the tribe's favored prey, and the Tribal Ban. So for example, a Bone Shadow initiation would involve hunting down a spirit to pay it in kind. Blood Talons would involve hunting another werewolf and not offering or accepting surrender unless under honorable terms. Iron masters would involve hunting a human in your territory without upsetting the territory's natural state. Etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T08:10:28-08:00","id":823358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neckbeard the Pirate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/822169-how-exclusive-is-tribe-membership-in-2e?p=822629#post822629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So joining a tribe would involve presenting yourself before the tribal totem and getting their approval? I always got the sense of them being rather distant and hard to reach, but maybe that was just a fault in my reading. Exactly how easy is it to make contact with one of them?</div> </div> </div> </div> There are spirit courts. There are examples in 1e books about members of the Totem spirit courts visiting members and prospective members of the Tribes. So, that could still happen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}